<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $44.6 mln Oct 30.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $44.6 mln Oct 30.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $44.6 million surplus on October 30 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 30</p>
<p>Exports: $182.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $187.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $207.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $158.1 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $44.6 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.529 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.933 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $6.302 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $4.133 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.765 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
